### Describe the bug

Hi there, 

In if block, throwing an error after `return undefined` makes whole `if` block is omitted.

Please see the input code and playground for detail.

I've been experincing this issue since I updated my nextjs version.
I checked the issue is reproducible @1.3.14 **when compress is on**.

Thanks in advance.

### Input code

```typescript
const fn = () => {
  let val;

  if (!val) {
    return undefined;
    // works as expected if comment out below line
    throw new Error('first');
  }

  if (val.a?.b !== true) { // Uncaught TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'a')
    throw new Error('second');
  }
  return val;
}
```


